PlayWright
-----------------------------------------------
1. playwright is webbased functional automation tool like selenium, cypress
2. Playwright supports -> webbased application, Mobile Web apps, API, doest not support mobile native apps
3. playwright -> langugage supports - javascript, typescript, java, python, .net(c#) 
4. Browser Supports -> Chromium based browser, Webkit - Safari
5. OS Supported -> Window, MacOS, Linux and supports CLI (command line intepreter)


Feature of playwright
1. free and Open Source.
2. Multiple Browser and OS
3. Very Easy installation.
4. Functional, Api, and accessiblity testing supports
5. CI-CD, Docker
6. parallel - testing
7. Auto wait mechanism - wait
8. build in assertions.
9. Multi tab and Multi window feature is available in playwright.
10. Frames and shadow DOM element supports playwright.
11. parameterization
12. Mobile emulates supports available
13. Fast



How to run the test in plawright
1. npx playwright test  | headless mode.  | run all test in all browser in headless mode
2. npx playwright test --headed   | run all test in all browser in headed mode.
3. to open report | npx playwright show-report 
4. npx playwright test filename (filename.spec.js)  | run specific spec file from test folder.
5. npx playwright test filename --project= chromium  | run test on specific browser.(chromium, webkit, chrome,firefox)
6. npx playwright test filename --project=chromium --headed --debug | enable and run test in debug mode




to create test in playwright, we need to import view packages from playwright.

import {test,expect} from '@plawright/test'

1. console.log('A')
2. console.log('B')
3. console.log('C')

async: this command tell javascript we need to wait for few method which cannot finished ther task immideately
await: makes command wait unit it recives the output from previous command.



Locators in Playwright
1. property -- element would have many properties, class, name, id, href
2. css
3. xpath

page.locator('property/css/xpath')

format options to write function.

page.locator('locator').click()   // playwright
page.click('locator')  // javascript.

Assisgnment for everyone
1. look for an website
2. look for an element which having an title attribute.
3. put validation against element.
page.getByTitle() :to locate an element by its title attribute.

// two method to get the text of an element
1. textCotent();
2. innerText();


To record the scripts in playwright follow below commands
1. npx playwright codegen - enables record tool and browser.
2. npx playwright codegen -o tests/myTest.spec.js | record scripts directly into thefile.
3. npx playwright codegen --target javascripts  | record scripts with targeted language.
4. npx playwright codegen -b webkit | safari | chromium
5. npx playwright codegen --device "iPhone 13"
6. npx playwright tests/filename.spec.js | command to run on mobile device (emulator/ simulator)
7. npx playwright codegen --device "iPhone XX" | return the full list of b/device in response.

